course: dictionary
lesson: 8808
title: Finding meaning from context: sheaf
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which one. Read the words before and after the tricky word and ask what would make sense there. «Joseph dreamed that his brothers' sheaves of corn, and the sun, moon and stars, bowed down to him, and he told them.» Corn grows as tall stalks, and you can cut them and tie them up. So a sheaf of corn must be a bundle of corn stalks.
explain: Check your idea by swapping in a simple meaning. Does "bundle of corn stalks" fit? Yes, it does. Now look at the other meaning: «a sheaf of papers» is a thick pile of papers held together. The word "of" is a clue. A sheaf is a bundle of something, and the something tells you what kind of bundle it is.
explain: Pictures and events can give clues too. At harvest festival, a sheaf of wheat is often shown to say thank you for the harvest. Sheaves of wheat or bread shaped like one are part of that happy day. When context is not enough, check a dictionary.
fact: A sheaf is a bundle of stalks of wheat, barley or other grain, tied together after cutting at harvest.
fact: A sheaf of papers is a thick pile or bundle of papers.
fact: The plural of sheaf is sheaves.
fact: Sheaves of wheat are often displayed at harvest festival to give thanks for the harvest.
fact: In the Bible, Joseph dreams that his brothers' sheaves bow down to his sheaf.
exercise: «Joseph dreamed that his brothers' sheaves of corn bowed down to him.» What is a sheaf of corn? | A dish of cooked corn | *A bundle of corn stalks tied together after cutting | A small bird that lives in fields | A tall grain silo
exercise: Mrs Hale carries «a sheaf of papers» to class. What does sheaf mean here? | A pencil case | *A thick pile or bundle of papers | A folder with a lock | A single sheet of paper
exercise: Copy the plural of sheaf from «Joseph dreamed that his brothers' sheaves of corn bowed down to him.» | *sheaves | dreamed | brothers | corn
test: What is a sheaf of wheat? | A field of wheat that is growing | A sheet of paper | A bread with a hole in the middle | *A bundle of wheat stalks tied together after cutting
test: Why might a school display a sheaf of wheat at harvest festival? | *To give thanks for the harvest | To hold up the classroom door | To show a new football | To build a tent
exam: Which clue in «Joseph dreamed that his brothers' sheaves of corn bowed down to him» best helps you work out what sheaf means? | Bowed down | Joseph's dream | *Sheaves of corn, which are things that are cut from a field and tied up | The sun, moon and stars
